# Azure DevOps parses this file with its own YAML engine, and Prettier's YAML
# printer reflows long values onto continuation lines. That is what broke the
# pipeline: the Docker `arguments` values became multi-line plain scalars that
# begin with `--`, which Azure DevOps reads as a sequence entry and rejects with
# "There was a YAML error preventing Azure Pipelines from determining if the
# pipeline should run". Keep this file out of formatting runs and edit it by hand.
azure-pipelines.yml
